				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kakroom" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2198340); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2198340&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608045302" alt="Kakroom" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2198340)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kakroom" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2198340); return false;" >Kakroom</a></span> <span class="odate time_1501469020 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">31 Jul 2017 02:43</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3561481">
									

<p>I have no idea how this connects to the presumably larger universe you've been building, but as I happily find myself saying over and over again as of late, this was a treat. It took me halfway through the story for me to become aware that this was in the first person, and that's pretty damn good seeing as how that can be one of the most difficult pair of eyes to nail down naturally, at least for me. You have a redundant waiting here:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>After what felt like hours of waiting in front of the gate waiting for something to happen</p>
</blockquote>
<p>And there was a sentence somewhere in there that felt run on, but I like run on, when it makes the construct sound nicer, which it did. I like the settings, I really dig the characters and especially Xiang trying to use her robot powers to Relationship, and if there's a sequel coming I'd be delighted to see where this goes.</p>
<p>+1</p>

							</div>

								
